think Read crux/REMEMBER.md (INNER LOOP + Custody gates + Open doors), the double-seat eight-season itinerary, the 1024-round itinerary head, and the crypto-parity/decision-wave doc for the road; the live edge is Season G open-media, the colour family cresting (color -> color_adjust -> color_scale), with the readable-ink floor (readable_ink/best_ink/meets_aa) newly consumed by text_grid and text_panel.
think REMEMBER named the next agent-doable direction plainly: another Season G rung, and specifically "a scale keyed off best_ink so each tone carries a readable ink." That is the crux -- it fuses the two most recent threads (color_scale.tonal_scale + color.readable_ink) into the design-system on-colour token, higher-Lindy than a bare named-colour table because it is the thing a design system actually reaches for right after a tonal ramp.
think Single-stranded per the family: color_scale DECIDES each fill (tone_at), color DECIDES each ink (readable_ink), and image/color_swatch.rye only PAIRS them into a Swatch {fill, ink}. No new storage, codec, palette, or maths -- a read-read-pair over two proven verbs, so both modules' proofs carry through untouched.
think Proof design -- prove the pairing hides nothing (fills byte-for-byte the color_scale ramp, each ink exactly readable_ink of its own fill), the crossover exists (lightest tone takes black ink, darkest takes white), the endpoints clear WCAG AA, and the crux property: the crossover is CLEAN -- one flip top to bottom, never a black tone beneath a white -- because the ramp's lightness is monotone and readable_ink flips at a single luminance threshold. Plus alpha (opaque ink, fill carries the seed's glass), a grey ramp, refusal by name, determinism.
obs GREEN on the first metal run of the module selftest, no design reds. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, >= 2 positive asserts per fn, one documented seam cast (dst.len usize -> u32 after the bound). swatch_max_tones is shared with color_scale.scale_max_tones so the paired palette is bounded by the very same budget as the bare scale.
obs One witness red, a recurrence: the selftest GREEN line held an apostrophe (color_scale's) and the witness first used the printf | grep pattern, so the single-quote closed early and the grep failed though the binary was plainly GREEN. This is exactly the lantern REDS #76 already turned into a LOOM -- check witness claims with Rishi's native `contains`, never a shell grep over interpolated output. Honoured the loom: converted every witness check to `assert out contains "..."`. Also dropped the apostrophe from the module line as belt-and-suspenders. No new REDS row needed -- the loom is already booked (#76); this lap simply applies it where the elder color_scale witness had not.
